Error: Jet.UseAfterMove: `counter` was consumed by a task that captures it, so it can't be used here
  --> Tests/UI/ConcurrencyBoundaries/task_takes_a_writing_function_value_its_owner_calls_again.jet:12:11
    |
 12 |     print(counter(2))
    |           ^^^^^^^
  --> Tests/UI/ConcurrencyBoundaries/task_takes_a_writing_function_value_its_owner_calls_again.jet:11:18
    |
 11 |     worker: task counter(1)
    |                  ^^^^^^^^^^ `counter` moved to a task that captures it here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `counter` after the move, or spawn the task in a `task.group`, whose child borrows `counter` until the join: a function value has no copy to give.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.UseAfterMove
